WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.670
This is the big day! You will plan and give your very first speech, using everything you have learned.

2
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.320
Choose something you can talk about happily.

3
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:15.570
My hero, a fun day I will never forget, or why I love cricket, dance or books.

4
00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:18.300
If you love it, your listeners will feel it.

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.220
A speech has an opening, three main points and a closing.

6
00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:26.760
Write key words for each part, not every word.

7
00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.560
It is your map, so you will not get lost.

8
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:35.890
Practise once alone, once in front of a mirror or camera, and once for a friend or family member.

9
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.020
Each time, look at your map a little less.

10
00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.180
Take a deep breath and smile before you begin.

11
00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:47.030
Stand tall, speak slowly and pause between your points.

12
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:49.000
If you forget, look at your map, breathe, and carry on.

13
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.900
Listen to Riya give her speech about her hero.

14
00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:57.610
Who is your hero? Mine is my grandmother.

15
00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.680
First, she is very kind. She feeds the stray dogs on our street every morning.

16
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.720
Second, she is brave. She learned to ride a scooter when she was sixty!

17
00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:12.680
Third, she tells the best stories. That is why my grandmother is my hero. Thank you for listening!

18
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.280
Riya used a speech map, just like our show and tell, but bigger.

19
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.470
She opened with a question. Then she gave three points, each with an example.

20
00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:27.520
She used first, second and third, so we always knew where we were.

21
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.880
She closed with, that is why, and thank you for listening.

22
00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:35.440
Feeling nervous is normal. Even famous speakers get butterflies in their tummy.

23
00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.610
Breathe in slowly for four counts, and out for four counts. Then smile.

24
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:46.510
If you forget a line, just look at your map, take a breath and carry on.

25
00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:50.320
Remember, everyone in the room wants you to do well.

26
00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:53.680
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

27
00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:57.350
Now plan it, build it, test it, and share it!
